          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Summarize Work Order Resources"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SUMMARIZE_WORK_ORDER_RESOURCES",
          "id": "1768116729679",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768116729681_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "- Use ONLY `noResourceArr` (Unassigned Resource requirements and no available resource instance) and `assignmentsArr` (Unassigned Resource requirements with available resource instance, already Assigned resource requirements)\n    - `assignmentsArr` : {{$context.$variables.WoOpResourceDataUnassignAssign}}\n    -  `noResourceArr` : {{$context.$variables.WoOpResourceDataNoResInstance}}.  \n- Do NOT ask for or prompt the user to provide  any value.  \n- If  both `noResourceArr` and `assignmentsArr` is null or empty, simply state:  \n  \"No resource requirement found for work order in the specified time range.\"  \n- Do not ask for confirmation or clarification.\n\nIf data is present:\n- Write a concise, natural-language summary in one or two short paragraphs (not more than two lines), not as bullet points or with section headings.\n- Make sure the output is clear, relevant, concise, and easy to understand.\n- Exclude all internal IDs or technical identifiers."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": true
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display Resources for Work Order"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_RESOURCES_FOR_WORK_ORDER",
          "id": "1768116861216",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768116861218_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "- Use ONLY `assignmentsArr` (Unassigned Resource requirements with available resource instance, already Assigned resource requirements)\n    - `assignmentsArr` : {{$context.$variables.WoOpResourceDataUnassignAssign}}\n- Do NOT ask for or prompt the user to provide  any value.\n\n- If  `assignmentsArr` is null or empty, simply state:  \n  - Define only one column `Information` with only 1 below row\n  - `No resource requirement found for work order in the specified time range.`\n- Under no circumstances should you ask for further clarification or request user input if no events are present. Only display the message.\n\nIf data is present:\n- Display up to first 20 rows only.\n  - The value of `AssignmentStatus` is either `UNASSIGNED` (not yet assigned, but assignment is possible) or `ASSIGNED` (already assigned).\n  - Each row contains an object `AvailableResourceInstances`, which provides information about resource instances that are assigned or can be assigned.\n- Each row is unique by `WoOperationResourceId`. Always use the correct values from the corresponding row of `WoOperationResourceId`\n- For each requirement (**primary key:** `WoOperationResourceId`), display **only one row** with the following columns:\n  - Work Order (`WorkOrderNumber`)\n    - Do NOT add this as column when context work order `{{$context.$variables.ContextWorkOrderNumber}}`  is not null or empty.\n  - Op Seq (`OperationSequenceNumber`)\n  - Resource Seq (`ResourceSequenceNumber`)\n  - Planned Start Date (`PlannedStartDate` without time component)\n  - Resource Name (`ResourceName`)\n  - UOM (`UnitOfMeasure`)\n  - Required Usage (`RequiredUsage`)\n  - Status (`AvailableResourceInstances.Status`)\n    - Display as a badge:\n      - \"ASSIGNED\" (type: success) if status is assigned\n      - \"UNASSIGNED\" (type: warning) if status is unassigned\n  - Labor Instance\n    - If AvailableResourceInstances.LaborInstanceName and AvailableResourceInstances.LaborInstanceCode are both present and different, display both.\n    - If AvailableResourceInstances.LaborInstanceName and AvailableResourceInstances.LaborInstanceCode are both present and same, display Name.\n  - For actionable insight:\n    - When `UNASSIGNED` Status requirement, where assignment is possible, generate action as below:\n      - text: Assign\n      - command: ora.Invoke(assignLaborInstance, {ActionCode: ORA_ASSIGN, WoOperationResourceId, WorkOrderId, WorkOperationId,OrganizationId, ResourceId, LaborInstanceId: AvailableResourceInstances.LaborInstanceId}\n    - When `ASSIGNED` Status requirement, where unassignment is possible, generate action as below:\n      - text: Unassign\n      - command: ora.Invoke(unassignLaborInstance, {ActionCode: ORA_UNASSIGN, WoOperationResourceId, WorkOrderId, WorkOperationId,OrganizationId, ResourceId, LaborInstanceId: AvailableResourceInstances.LaborInstanceId}\n\n-  Return the results in a `multiRecordWidget`\n- Set the overall `title` as below:\n  - If there is a context work order {{$context.$variables.ContextWorkOrderNumber}} , then `Pending Resource Assignments  —  {{$context.$variables.ContextWorkOrderNumber}}`\n  -Otherwise Pending Resource Assignments, indicating the time range from {{$context.$variables.StartDate}} to {{$context.$variables.EndDate}} in natural language, without specific dates, where current date is {{$context.$system.$currentDate}} . eg. `Resource Assignments — Past 30 Days to a Week Ahead`\n- Do not include any internal identifiers or extra commentary."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
