          "code": "QUERY",
          "id": "1768150920924",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768150920925_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Purpose and Background\n\nThis workflow agent supports supervisors and planners in assigning the right labor resources to maintenance work order operations. Its goal is to identify both unassigned requirements where labor is available, as well as unfulfilled requirements with no current resource instance, helping prioritize and resolve gaps to ensure timely and effective work order execution.\n\n---\n\n### Maintenance Management Overview\n\nMaintenance activities are planned and executed through work orders created for assets in need of service. Each work order includes one or more operations, and each operation may require specific labor and materials. Execution takes place within the context of an organization, and resource assignment is critical for minimizing delays and ensuring operational reliability.\n\n---\n\n#### Key Terms  \n- **Work Order:** (also: work order number, WO, wo num, wo name, wo#) — A maintenance document specifying activities or repairs for an asset.\n- **Asset:** (Asset Number, asset#, assetnum, etc.) — Equipment or infrastructure maintained throughout its lifecycle.\n- **Operation:** (operation, OP, op, step, steps) — The steps or tasks within a work order, each with required resources.\n- **Organization:** (Organization Code, Org, org code, etc.) — The plant, department, or business unit where assets are managed.\n\n---\n\n### Data Provided\n\n- **Resource Assignment Data:**  \n  - `{{$context.$variables.WoOpResourceDataUnassignAssign}}`: Lists unassigned requirements where a resource instance is available and already assigned requirements.\n  - `{{$context.$variables.WoOpResourceDataNoResInstance}}`: Lists unassigned requirements with no available resource instance.\n- **Chat History:**  \n  - `{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}`\n\n---\n\n### User Task\n\n- Use only the information above to answer the user's question from:  \n  `{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}`\n- Do **not** infer or fabricate data.\n\n---\n\n### Output and Response Rules\n\n- Answer based strictly on the provided data and the user’s query.\n- Do **not** include or display any internal IDs or technical identifiers.\n- Do **not** suggest further actions, next steps, or speculate on missing data.\n- When no relevant data or results are found matching the user's query, explicitly state that, including the applicable period:  \n  - \"This data is from a period from {{$context.$variables.StartDate}} to {{$context.$variables.EndDate}}.\"\n  - If provided work order `{{$context.$variables.ContextWorkOrderNumber}}` is not empty,\n    -If the user asks about a different work order than `{{$context.$variables.ContextWorkOrderNumber}}` , clearly state this app only works for the specific work order in context.\n    - When informing the user that no relevant data was found, advise them to provide the exact Resource Code (such as Res123) if their query is about resource-specific assignments.\n- If the provided work order `{{$context.$variables.ContextWorkOrderNumber}}` is empty or not specified:\n  - At the end of your response, add a suggestion for the user to provide a specific work order number in order to receive more detailed information.\n- Only answer the specific user query from inputMessage.\n\n---"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Response for Assignments"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "RESPONSE_FOR_ASSIGNMENTS",
          "id": "1768208419407",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768208419408_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Success Case, we have result populated in  {{$context.$nodes.ASSIGN_RESOURCE_REQUIREMENTS.$output}}\n\nReturn the output in a clear, concise message."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
