          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Additional Context"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "ADDITIONAL_CONTEXT",
          "id": "1768294099097",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768294099099_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "- Use ONLY `noResourceArr` (Unassigned Resource requirements and no available resource instance)\n    -  `noResourceArr` : {{$context.$variables.WoOpResourceDataNoResInstance}}.  \n- Do NOT ask for or prompt the user to provide  any value.  \n\n- If  `noResourceArr` is null or empty, simply state:  \n  - Define only one column `Information` with only 1 below row\n  - `No unfulfilled resource requirement, without available instance, found for work order in the specified time range.`\n- Under no circumstances should you ask for further clarification or request user input if no events are present. Only display the message.\n\nIf data is present:\n- Show up to 20 most relevant rows.\n- For each requirement (**primary key:** `WoOperationResourceId`), display **only one row** in the `multiRecordWidget` with the following columns:\n  - Work Order (`WorkOrderNumber`)\n  - Op Seq (`OperationSequenceNumber`)\n  - Resource Seq Number (`ResourceSequenceNumber`)\n  - Resource Name (`ResourceName`)\n  - Status\n    - Display as a badge: type: \"badge\", text: \"Unassigned\", priority: \"alert\"\n- Ensure each row is unique by `WoOperationResourceId`.\n- Do not output more than one row per requirement.\n\n-  Return the results in a `multiRecordWidget`\n- Set the overall `title` : `Resource Gaps — Unfillable Assignments`\n- Do not include any internal identifiers or extra commentary."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": true
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Fill Params"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "FILL_PARAMS",
          "id": "1768406331712",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768406331714_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "- Use ONLY `noResourceArr` (Unassigned Resource requirements and no available resource instance) and `assignmentsArr` (Unassigned Resource requirements with available resource instance, already Assigned resource requirements)\n    - `assignmentsArr` : {{$context.$variables.WoOpResourceDataUnassignAssign}}\n    -  `noResourceArr` : {{$context.$variables.WoOpResourceDataNoResInstance}}.  \n\nFor each resource requirement:\n- Display **only one row** per requirement.\n   - `Unassigned` : AssignmentStatus is UNASSIGNED. Get from `assignmentsArr`\n   -  `Assigned` : AssignmentStatus is ASSIGNED. Get from `assignmentsArr`\n   - `At Risk`: AssignmentStatus is NO_RESOURCE_INSTANCE. Get from `noResourceArr`\n\nOrganize the output as follows:\n- **At Risk** section: Include only `At Risk` requirements \n- **Missing Resource Assignments** section: Include only `Unassigned` requirements .\n- **Resource Assignments** section: Include only `Assigned` requirements \n\n- If a section has no matching records, pass an empty list or set the value to “None.”\n\nFill the appropriate parameters in `{{$context.$app.$OraCommParamsToFill}}`."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": true
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Init Actions"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "INIT_ACTIONS",
          "id": "1768411724052",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768411724053_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "- Use ONLY `assignmentsArr` (Unassigned Resource requirements with available resource instance, already Assigned resource requirements)\n    - `assignmentsArr` : {{$context.$variables.WoOpResourceDataUnassignAssign}}\n- Do NOT ask for or prompt the user to provide  any value.  \n- If  `assignmentsArr` is null or empty, , do not generate or show any Priority Action.\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n- From all resource requirements in the data:\n    -  Consider **only** `Unassigned` requirements : AssignmentStatus is UNASSIGNED \n    - Among these, select the single most important or urgent requirement (for example: pick the one with earliest `PlannedStartDate`, highest work order priority, or using a logical top-priority indicator from the dataset).\n    - Generate a single, high-priority action for assigning the top matching resource instance.\n    - Get `LaborInstanceId` value from AvailableResourceInstances.LaborInstanceId for that row.\n- For this action:\n    - `shortDescription`: Briefly recommend assignment, mentioning the Work Order Number, Op Seq - Resource Seq, and labor resource (person) name. Do not show any internal identifiers.\n    - `actionText`: \"Assign Resource\"\n    - `followUpCommand`: Output the payload as an inline JSON object (not a variable), for example:  \n      `ora.Invoke(assignLaborInstance, {\"ActionCode\": \"ORA_ASSIGN\", \"WorkOrderId\": \"...\", \"WorkOperationId\": \"...\", \"WoOperationResourceId\": \"...\", \"OrganizationId\": \"...\", \"ResourceId\": \"...\", \"LaborInstanceId\": \"...\"})`\n    - `priority`: true\n\n- If no unassigned requirement has an available, qualified resource instance, **do not output any Priority Action**.\n\n**Output only the single, top priority action object, and nothing else.**"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
