        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract Work Order Data from User Query"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771228566549"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACT_WORK_ORDER_DATA_FROM_USER_QUERY",
          "id": "1771228376583",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771228376585_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Extract data from the user query: `{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}` and build a valid Oracle REST Query Language (RQL) syntax  `q` parameter (`pQparam`) for searching work orders, which can be directly used in a REST call.\n\n**Build `pQparam` as follows:**\n- If `OrganizationId` having value (`{{$context.$variables.ContextOrganizationId}}`) is not empty, MUST always include the below clause:  \n  `OrganizationId = {{$context.$variables.ContextOrganizationId}}`\n- If `WorkOrderNumber` having value (` {{$context.$variables.ContextWorkOrderNumber}}`) is not empty, MUST include the clause:  \n  `WorkOrderNumber = '{{$context.$variables.ContextWorkOrderNumber}}'`\n- If `WorkOrderNumber` is empty, include below `PlannedStartDate` clause:\n  `(PlannedStartDate BETWEEN '{{$context.$variables.StartDate}}' AND '{{$context.$variables.EndDate}}' )`\n- For BETWEEN clauses, always use parentheses and dates in 'YYYY-MM-DD' format. \n- The current date `CurrentDate` value is `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`. \n- Extract relevant parameter values and construct `pQparam` using valid Oracle REST Query Language (RQL) syntax.\n\n**Important Constraints:**\n- When both `OrganizationId` and `WorkOrderNumber` are available, join with `AND`, and append any additional search criteria requested by the user after those mandatory clauses.\n- For questions about unassigned resources or missing assignments, **never** include assignment or resource fulfillment logic in the q param—only use fields/filters natively supported by the WorkOrder REST API.\n  - Business logic for unassigned or unfulfilled resource instances will be applied later and never in this q parameter.\n- Do **not** include explanations or errors. **Always return a valid query string.**\n\n**Examples:**  \n1) Get requirements gaps (Both `OrganizationId` and `WorkOrderNumber` are not empty))\n`pQparam` = \"OrganizationId = 123456 AND WorkOrderNumber ='JKJWO1'\"\n2) Get all labor information for work order that starts with JKJ WO 001 and having resource requirement for  I-Inspector (Only `OrganizationId` is not empty)\n`pQparam` = \"OrganizationId = 123456 AND WorkOrderNumber like UPPER('JKJ WO 001%25')  AND WorkOrderOperation.WorkOrderOperationResource.ResourceCode = 'I-Inspector' AND (PlannedStartDate BETWEEN '2025-09-02' AND '2025-03-18')\"\n3) Get information on resource I-Inspector for work orders in last 1 month (Only `WorkOrderNumber` is not empty)\n`pQparam` = \"WorkOrderNumber ='JKJ WO 001' AND WorkOrderOperation.WorkOrderOperationResource.ResourceCode = 'I-Inspector'\"\n4) Example for a complex pQparam\n`pQparam` = \"UPPER(WorkOrderNumber) like UPPER('aBc%25') AND (AssetNumber = 'Asset_001' OR AssetNumber = 'Asset_003' ) AND WorkOrderDescription like 'ABC Wo%25' AND WorkOrderTypeCode != 'CORRECTIVE' AND WorkOrderSubTypeCode=UPPER('ora_planned') AND WorkOrderStatusCode IN ('ORA_RELEASED','ORA_UNRELEASED') AND (PlannedStartDate BETWEEN '2025-03-07' and '2026-06-24' ) AND WorkOrderOperation.OperationSequenceNumber = 10 AND WorkOrderOperation.WorkOrderOperationResource.ResourceCode IS NULL AND attachments.DocumentPreviewURL IS NOT NULL AND WorkOrderOperation.WorkOrderOperationMaterial.InventoryItemNumber = 'm-assy-srl-p'\"\n\nReturn **only** the constructed `pQparam` string, and nothing else."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"pQparam\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
