          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771228630033",
              "name": "CsvListOfWorkOrder",
              "scope": "JOB",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.GET_WORK_ORDERS_FROM_USER_QUERY.$output?.items && $context.$nodes.GET_WORK_ORDERS_FROM_USER_QUERY.$output.items.length > 0 ? $context.$nodes.GET_WORK_ORDERS_FROM_USER_QUERY.$output.items.map(item => \"'\" + item.WorkOrderNumber + \"'\").join(\",\")  : \"'_'\"}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SET_FIELDS"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Unwrap the Loop Output",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const raw = $context?.$nodes?.FOR_EACH_RESOURCE_REQUIREMENT?.$output ?? [];\n\nconst objectsArr = (Array.isArray(raw) ? raw : [])\n  .map(s => { try { return JSON.parse(String(s)); } catch { return null; } })\n  .map(o => o?.result)\n  .filter(r => r != null);\n\n\nconst assignmentsArr = objectsArr\n  .filter(o => o?.AssignmentStatus === 'UNASSIGNED' || o?.AssignmentStatus === 'ASSIGNED')\n  .sort((a, b) => {\n    const rank = s => (s === 'UNASSIGNED' ? 0 : s === 'ASSIGNED' ? 1 : 2);\n    return rank(a?.AssignmentStatus) - rank(b?.AssignmentStatus);\n  });\n\nconst noResourceArr = objectsArr\n  .filter(o => o?.AssignmentStatus === 'NO_RESOURCE_INSTANCE');\n\nreturn { assignmentsArr, noResourceArr };"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1768131701852"
          },
          "code": "UNWRAP_THE_LOOP_OUTPUT",
          "id": "1771508417706",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": true
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Suggested Communication"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SUGGESTED_COMMUNICATION",
          "id": "1771822622681",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771822622682_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "- Use `assignmentsArr` (Unassigned Resource requirements with available resource instance, already Assigned resource requirements)\n    - `assignmentsArr` : {{$context.$variables.WoOpResourceDataUnassignAssign}}\n- Use `noResourceArr` (Unassigned Resource requirements and no available resource instance)\n    -  `noResourceArr` : {{$context.$variables.WoOpResourceDataNoResInstance}}.  \n- Do NOT ask for or prompt the user to provide  any value.\n\n-Generate an automated email highlighting following:\n- `title`: Resource Fulfillment Summary` \n- `description`: Provide a one-sentence summary of the findings.\n- `actionText`: Send\n- Email content should include\n  - Recommend that the recipient reviews these resource requirements and resources instances availability, and take appropriate action. \n  - Include Work Order Number, Operation Seq Num, Resoure Seq Num, Resource name, Labor Resource Instance Name/Person Name and other appropriate values in the email.\n   - At Risk requirements from `noResourceArr`, if available.\n   - Unfulfilled resource requirement from `assignmentsArr`\n   - Assigned resource requirement from `assignmentsArr`\n- Write the email content using rich text and include appropriate HTML tags for formatting (such as `<b>`, `<ul>`, `<li>`, etc.).\n\nReturn only the completed email with HTML formatting, ready to send."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
